        <h2 class="text-2xl md:text-3xl font-serif text-navy-900 mt-12 mb-4">How insurance IDV depreciation compares to actual resale market value</h2>

        <p>Two systems assign value to the same car. They almost never agree.</p>

        <p>
          IDV, or Insured Declared Value, is the maximum amount an insurance company pays if the car is stolen or written off in an accident. IRDAI (Insurance Regulatory and Development Authority of India) mandates a depreciation schedule that insurers use to calculate IDV. The schedule follows a fixed percentage based on the car's age:
        </p>

        <div class="overflow-x-auto my-6">
          <table class="w-full text-base border border-cream-200 bg-white">
            <thead class="bg-cream-100">
